// REQUIRES: uv
// RUN: zkc-opt %pir-seal-full %pir-project-full %S/../Encoding/sumcheck.mlir > %t.mlir
// RUN: zkc-run %t.mlir --vectors %S/Inputs/sumcheck-exec-vectors.json | FileCheck %s
//
// Execution parity for the first claim-DAG protocol: the projected
// sumcheck verifier replays the oracle-generated golden vectors
// bit-exactly. The vectors walk the reject surface round by round —
// an honest proof against an inflated claim dies before any challenge
// is squeezed; a tampered round-2 message dies between the challenges;
// the round-consistent cheat survives every local check and dies at
// the final evaluation with both challenges on the transcript. The
// committed vector file is the cross-implementation execution
// contract; the uv-gated lines below regenerate it from the oracle
// and require byte identity.
//
// RUN: %uv python -m oracle.exec sumcheck > %t.vectors
// RUN: diff %t.vectors %S/Inputs/sumcheck-exec-vectors.json
//
// CHECK: honest: accept [1654834368763198252,960454384712253740]
// CHECK-NEXT: false_statement: check_failure []
// CHECK-NEXT: tampered_message: check_failure [1654834368763198252]
// CHECK-NEXT: consistent_cheat: check_failure [829048626563406359,2221636072341486221]
// CHECK-NEXT: trailing_byte: proof_trailing_data [1654834368763198252,960454384712253740]
// CHECK-NEXT: truncated: abi_decode_failure [1654834368763198252]
// CHECK-NEXT: noncanonical_value: abi_decode_failure []
